 - The retry path needs a live provider and is not unit-tested; the validator itself is (9 tests including a 500-case junk-input totality check).
 
 Suite: 74 / 74 (+16 this round).
+
+## 10. Game Bible compliance audit (v5)
+
+Method: each Bible section checked against code, with a test or a measured run where I could. **Met** = enforced and tested; **Partial** = exists but incomplete or unused by the live game; **Gap** = absent. Items changed in v5 are marked ▲.
+
+### §2 Pillars
+| Pillar | Status | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 Agency (5 choices + Intent) | Met ▲ | Five choices and free-form Intent in the store. v5: the narrator's choices are checked against what the rules can honour (invented destinations dropped) and backfilled by a deterministic generator. |
+| 2 Persistent causality | Partial ▲ | v5 finales make one resolved tension start the next (blockade → scarcity → rumors → lifted; assembly → schism → truce). No calendar/season/weather, and the world goes quiet after about turn 75 (see Gaps). |
+| 3 Living Jianghu | Partial | NPC agency is bounded (3 actions/tick) and acts offscreen. Faction `goals` are display strings that no code reads; factions only exert pressure (V3), they do not act. |
+| 4 Martial depth | **Gap** | Arts, techniques, mastery, requirements and counters exist as content only. The resolver never consults `techniqueId`, mastery, rank or Qi cost, and nothing teaches or advances an art. |
+| 5 Social consequence | Partial | Trust/respect/fear/affection/debt/grudge per relationship, memories, and obligations (V3 does enforce `dueTurn`). No Face (mianzi), no promises, reputation is one number per faction, not per region. |
+| 6 Fair uncertainty | Met ▲ | Resolution is deterministic; the narrator gets a perception-filtered digest and its `stateUpdates` are stripped. v5: rolls are seeded and replayable. |
+| 7 Wuxia first | Partial | World content is Wuxia-first with a switchable supernatural layer. The legacy `Spellbook` is mana-based and `Combat.tsx` is a separate, engine-free combat system. |
+| 8 Readable continuity | Partial | Simulation state (including seed, finale data, ledger) lives inside `GameState`, which the store persists. I did not test save/load through the persisted store. |
+
+### §4 Simulation contract
+| Requirement | Status | Evidence |
+|---|---|---|
+| LLM interprets intent into a structured action | **Gap** | Interpretation is a keyword table (`actionInterpreter.ts`); "bribe the guard" becomes `other`; NPC targets need the full name. |
+| Validate, resolve, reduce, log | Met | `resolveAction`: clone, validate before and after, ledger. |
+| Narration cannot grant items, change stats, move the player… | Met ▲ | v4 stripped all `stateUpdates` but a validated `locationChange`; v5 forces the authored start location for origin characters. |
+| AI unavailable ⇒ simulation still runs, fallback narrator | Met ▲ | **Was a violation:** a narrator error discarded the whole resolved turn. v5: `narrateResolvedTurn` commits the turn and uses `fallbackNarration` + `generateChoices`; demo mode does the same for origin characters. |
+| Injected, reproducible randomness | Met ▲ | **Was a gap:** default roll was `Math.random()` with no stored seed. v5: seed + draw counter in `world.rng`; roll N is a pure function of (seed, N); older saves get a seed on their first action. |
+
+### §5 State domains
+Present: Character, Jianghu/World events, NPC, Faction, Relationship, Knowledge, Economy (stock and scarcity). **Absent: QuestState, CombatState, TimeState.** `GameState.questLog` exists but nothing in the engine reads or writes it.
+
+### §6-7 Character, martial model, injury
+- Attributes, Qi and cultivation are modelled; martial-art data is complete in content but unused by rules (pillar 4).
+- Injuries have body regions, but the only source is one backlash on a high-risk failure and no injury changes any mechanic (a broken arm affects nothing).
+- **HP never decreases in the engine, so defeat cannot occur there.** Legacy `Combat.tsx` can reduce HP, and the store then shows an end screen; `revive()` restores half HP automatically, which §7 explicitly says not to use as the default. Defeat-as-new-situation (capture, ransom, debt) is not implemented.
+
+### §8-10 Social, living world, knowledge
+- NPC memory (event, interpretation, confidence) ✔; obligations ✔; knowledge split world/player/NPC with provenance ✔.
+- ▲ Finales plus `spread_rumor` mean offscreen events produce news the player can only learn by being there, hearing it from an NPC, or witnessing it.
+- **Rumors never move between locations** (`currentLocationId` is static; they spread only among NPCs already at the player's location), and they never mutate. Finales work around this by seeding the same news at several named locations.
+
+### §11 Time, travel, environment — **Gap**
+`world.turn` is the only clock. No hour, date, season, weather, travel duration or schedules. Travel costs a fixed turn regardless of distance even though the content pack defines a weighted graph.
+
+### §12-13 Interaction and AI roles
+| Role | Status |
+|---|---|
+| Narrator | Met: validated output, digest-only context, retry, deterministic fallback ▲ |
+| Choice generator | Partial ▲: deterministic and legal-by-construction (tested to interpret to the intended action); the LLM still proposes the primary list for origin characters |
+| Intent interpreter | Gap (keyword table; no ambiguity clarification) |
+| NPC dialogue | Partial: a voice line reaches the narrator; no separate contract that speaks from that NPC's knowledge |
+| World-event proposer | Gap |
+| Runtime schema validation | Met (v4) |
+| "Outcome explains what changed" | Partial: the ledger and digest hold it, but no screen shows costs and changes |
+
+### §14-16 Structure, roadmap, definition of done
+- Folder targets: `src/ai/` now holds `validateNarration`, `choiceGenerator`, `fallbackNarrator`; `src/world/content/` holds authored data. The engine is still flat rather than `actions/ simulation/ consequences/`; the §14 text says that is acceptable.
+- **§16 definition of done: met** (rejection before mutation, same state + action + roll ⇒ same result, no LLM in resolution, state validation at boundaries, no UI/storage/provider imports in `src/engine`, tests for success/failure/blocked/invalid roll/non-mutation).
+- Roadmap: M1 done. **M2 now substantially done** (adapter, validated JSON, safe fallback, narration cannot mutate); the only unmet M2 item is splitting intent interpretation out to its own model contract. M3 partial (Qi, injuries, relationships exist; mastery, sect rank, Face, promises do not). M4 partial (+ finales). M5 not started.
+
+### §18 Change control
+The Bible has not been updated to reflect decisions made since 1.0. They are recorded in `doc/DECISIONS.md` for you to merge or reject.
+
+## 11. v5 additions
+
+### Finale hooks (`src/engine/finale.ts`, `src/world/content/finales.ts`)
+- A world event can carry a `finale`: serializable data of ordered outcomes, each with conditions (player presence, player knowledge, faction tension/hostility, NPC alive/disposition, market scarcity) and effects (adjust faction / relation / NPC / market, add NPC goal, spread rumor at named locations, start a follow-up event). The first outcome whose conditions all hold wins; the last must be unconditional. No randomness, no LLM.
+- It fires when the event's causal chain completes (V4), ends the event, and emits `world.finale_resolved`. If the player is at the event's location they witness it: ledger witnesses, an `observation` knowledge record, and the narrator digest/fallback describe it. If not, nothing is told to them; the news exists only as rumors at the named places.
+- Cascades are bounded: `start_event` skips an id that already exists, so a finale chain cannot loop.
+- Digest foreshadowing: a local event with a finale says it will "come to a head very soon / before long" (deliberately fuzzy, never a countdown).
+- Seven authored finales (three seeded events plus four follow-ups), calibrated on a passive run: Toll Dispute → `ferry-blockade` (turn 21) → `blockade-lifted` (37); Fever Season → `fever-epidemic` (25) → `shortage-eased` (41); Autumn Assembly → `hall-schism` (49) → `uneasy-truce` (74). Engaging changes the outcome: being present with enough goodwill gives `toll-mediated` or `healer-rallied`, and being at Jade Hall knowing the volume is missing with Elder Bai's trust gives `volume-exposed`.
+- Goodwill decays while a faction dispute builds (stages 2-3), so trust has to be maintained: the integration test needs conversations both early and just before the finale.
+
+### Also in v5
+- `src/ai/fallbackNarrator.ts`, `src/ai/choiceGenerator.ts`, `src/engine/rng.ts`, and the store's `narrateResolvedTurn` (see §10).
+- `useIntent` now sends the digest for origin characters too (only `makeChoice` did before).
+- `llmService.narrate` throws if no usable narrative survives the retry, so the store can fall back.
+
+### Known limits of v5
+- After about turn 75 in passive play the seeded events are all resolved and nothing starts new ones; V3 only spawns faction-conflict events when hostility is at least 70. A world-event proposer (§13) is the missing piece.
+- Finale outcomes cannot kill an NPC, change a relationship's trust/respect separately from disposition, or start a quest.
+- Choice generation and fallback narration are tested against all six origins' first twelve turns, not against the full space of states.
+- Nothing here was played in a browser.
